  "placement": "Book page 79, topic 3.7 মহাকর্ষ বল: next to the text on the Earth's pull F = GmM/R² = mg and g = GM/R².",
  "order": 2,
  "maintainers": ["RadeenXALNW"],
  "units": "m",
  "description": "The falling apple (page 79, topic 3.7): an apple tree on a late-summer meadow, a young Newton reading under it, and five apples at 1 m to 5 m beside a height pole. The student lets an apple go: in slow motion it falls with the Earth's pull F on it, leaving a picture every 0.1 s, and the camera follows it down, then pulls back to show the trail. The formula F = G mM/R² is a live calculator: every symbol is a button (the apple, the arrow, the Earth from afar with R from its centre), sliders change m and h, F ÷ m stays g ≈ 9.8 ms⁻². Test tab: 5 tap questions. The two iron spheres and the cut-open Earth are the labs law-of-gravitation and law-of-gravitation-earth. Phone-first, Bangla and English.",
  "tags": ["force", "gravitation", "weight", "g", "apple", "formula", "bangla"],
  "params": [
    {
      "name": "lang",
      "label": "Language",
      "type": "select",
      "options": [["bn", "বাংলা"], ["en", "English"]],
      "default": "bn"
    },
    { "name": "m", "label": "Apple's mass (g)", "type": "number", "default": "200", "placeholder": "100–500" },
    { "name": "h", "label": "Height (m)", "type": "number", "default": "2", "placeholder": "1–5" },
    {
      "name": "t",
      "label": "Frozen moment of the fall (s)",
      "type": "number",
      "default": "",
      "placeholder": "empty: none",
      "help": "start frozen this many seconds into the fall, for pictures"
    },
    {
      "name": "steps",
      "label": "Falls already done",
      "type": "number",
      "default": "0",
      "placeholder": "0–1",
      "help": "1 starts after one fall, with the trail"
    },
    {
      "name": "sym",
      "label": "Symbol tapped",
      "type": "select",
      "options": [["", "none"], "F", "G", "m", "M", "R", "g"],
